 "notes": "The goal picture is /app/goal.png: the head camera's view (robot_r1:zed_link:Camera:0, same resolution and intrinsics) once the task is done. Simulated time passes only while the robot moves or you wait, and the episode has a fixed number of control steps (30 per simulated second; control_steps_left in every result): give short motions a short duration_s. Success needs the scene and the robot still for 45 control steps: after the last motion, wait at least 1.5 s. End-effector poses (goals and state) are the fingertip centre (TCP), midway between the two fingertips, about 2 cm further along the fingers than the end-effector frame between the finger pads, where a grasped object is held (the proprio eef_pose group). An end-effector goal is solved by the robot's inverse kinematics from the current joints and moves only that arm, in joint space, without collision checking. Grasping is assisted: closing on an object holds what the finger pads touch, and the hand lets go only when fully open (gripper 0). The reported gripper value is 1 while the measured opening is below 9 cm (closed, or holding an object) and 0 when fully open; gripper_opening_m is the measured opening. The cameras give RGB only (no depth). The simulator runs at about 8 control steps per second of wall time.",
